WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.631 --> 00:00:14.472
pulled on the door handle again and again.

2
00:00:15.552 --> 00:00:18.953
No matter how hard he pulled, the lab door still wouldn't open.

3
00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:20.994
"Pull harder!"

4
00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:22.094
said Waldo.

5
00:00:22.114 --> 00:00:23.354
"I am!"

6
00:00:24.275 --> 00:00:25.035
Ben grunted.

7
00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:28.596
"Why don't you try?"

8
00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:33.845
Waldo yanked on the door handle, but he couldn't open the door either.

9
00:00:33.865 --> 00:00:38.426
"It must be locked from the outside."

10
00:00:39.887 --> 00:00:41.287
Ben slumped against the door.

11
00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:46.108
"We'll never get out of here," he moaned.

12
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:48.429
He thought about Winnie.

13
00:00:49.429 --> 00:00:52.350
Then he thought about Winnie in her beautiful new black dress.

14
00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.231
By now she was probably back in the gym, looking for him.

15
00:00:56.251 --> 00:01:01.885
"Let me think," said Waldo, pacing back and forth.

16
00:01:01.905 --> 00:01:04.606
"There must be something we can do."

17
00:01:04.626 --> 00:01:08.067
"You're a wizard," said Ben.

18
00:01:08.087 --> 00:01:11.069
"Don't you know any spells that could open the door?"

19
00:01:12.209 --> 00:01:13.269
Waldo shook his head.

20
00:01:13.289 --> 00:01:15.430
"I left my spell book at home."

21
00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:17.651
Suddenly he laughed.

22
00:01:19.292 --> 00:01:19.772
"Wait a minute!

23
00:01:20.372 --> 00:01:21.553
Why are we worrying about this?

24
00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:23.434
You're a ghost, Ben.

25
00:01:24.034 --> 00:01:26.335
Just float through a wall and unlock the door!"

26
00:01:27.475 --> 00:01:28.256
Ben sighed.

27
00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:30.381
"I can't."

28
00:01:32.002 --> 00:01:33.343
Waldo's jaw dropped.

29
00:01:33.364 --> 00:01:36.046
"Are you kidding me?

30
00:01:37.407 --> 00:01:39.289
I thought all ghosts could float through walls.

31
00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:43.333
I mean, what's the point of being a ghost if you can't do stuff like that?"

32
00:01:44.654 --> 00:01:45.555
Ben was annoyed.

33
00:01:45.575 --> 00:01:48.598
"I never learned how, all right?

34
00:01:49.438 --> 00:01:50.840
And you're not helping us either.

35
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.064
What's the point of being a wizard if you can't even use magic to open a door?"

36
00:02:00.236 --> 00:02:00.756
"Good point."

37
00:02:01.556 --> 00:02:02.657
Waldo hung his head.

38
00:02:02.677 --> 00:02:04.377
"I'm sorry.

39
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.217
I was just annoyed.

40
00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.858
I don't want to miss the Monster Mash."

41
00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:10.739
"Me neither," said Ben.

42
00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:13.860
"I've really been looking forward to it."

43
00:02:17.081 --> 00:02:21.262
Waldo slid down next to Ben, and the two sat in silence for a moment.

44
00:02:27.603 --> 00:02:30.557
be able to float through walls eventually," Ben mumbled.

45
00:02:30.577 --> 00:02:37.281
"I practice every night, and my mom says that some ghosts just take longer than others to learn

46
00:02:37.321 --> 00:02:37.781
this stuff.

47
00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:40.043
Don't tell anyone, okay?"

48
00:02:40.063 --> 00:02:43.105
"I won't," Waldo promised.

49
00:02:43.125 --> 00:02:48.288
"I'm the only wizard I know who still needs to carry around a spell book.

50
00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:51.611
Really good wizards can do magic without spells."

51
00:02:55.633 --> 00:02:56.314
Ben replied.

52
00:02:57.875 --> 00:02:59.296
The two of them were quiet again.

53
00:03:01.244 --> 00:03:02.685
Then Ben heard something.

54
00:03:02.705 --> 00:03:05.846
"Footsteps!" he cried.

55
00:03:05.866 --> 00:03:08.027
"Waldo! Someone's coming!"

56
00:03:09.107 --> 00:03:11.908
They leaped to their feet as the footsteps came closer.

57
00:03:11.928 --> 00:03:16.110
"Everything is totally under control," said a voice.

58
00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:17.651
"It's Mr.

59
00:03:17.711 --> 00:03:19.011
Freaky," said Ben.

60
00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.112
"He can get us out of here!"

61
00:03:21.132 --> 00:03:24.733
"I'm really sorry, sir," another voice was saying.

62
00:03:24.753 --> 00:03:30.796
"Jen was getting ready for the dance, so I decided to wander around and explore Monster Academy.

63
00:03:31.368 --> 00:03:32.689
I didn't think I'd get lost."

64
00:03:33.729 --> 00:03:34.810
Waldo looked at Ben.

65
00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:37.551
"That must be Jen's date," he said.

66
00:03:37.571 --> 00:03:39.151
"The human."

67
00:03:40.432 --> 00:03:41.192
Ben nodded.

68
00:03:41.212 --> 00:03:44.013
"It's fine," Mr.

69
00:03:44.053 --> 00:03:45.134
Freaky said to the boy.

70
00:03:45.154 --> 00:03:47.255
"I'm just glad I found you.

71
00:03:48.175 --> 00:03:51.356
It's not a good idea to have a human wandering around alone.

72
00:03:52.257 --> 00:03:53.717
You might scare one of the monsters."

73
00:03:53.737 --> 00:03:55.738
"Mr. Freaky, help!"

74
00:03:56.118 --> 00:03:59.560
Ben shouted, "We're trapped in the science lab!"

75
00:04:00.724 --> 00:04:01.565
"Let us out!"

76
00:04:02.005 --> 00:04:03.366
Waldo pounded on the door.

77
00:04:03.386 --> 00:04:05.066
"We're locked in!"

78
00:04:06.047 --> 00:04:07.908
Mr. Freaky didn't seem to hear them.

79
00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:12.270
"This will be a wonderful dance, young man," the principal was saying.

80
00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.872
"I think you're going to enjoy dancing with our monster students.

81
00:04:16.713 --> 00:04:19.795
And there's even another human here tonight—Mrs.

82
00:04:19.835 --> 00:04:21.335
Hubbletree, the mayor's wife!"

83
00:04:22.536 --> 00:04:25.778
A moment later the principal's voice faded down the hallway.

84
00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:27.879
"Help! We're trapped!"

85
00:04:28.379 --> 00:04:29.280
yelled Ben again.

86
00:04:30.508 --> 00:04:30.989
But Mr.

87
00:04:31.049 --> 00:04:31.949
Freaky was gone.

88
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.672
Ben turned to Waldo in disbelief.

89
00:04:35.612 --> 00:04:36.753
"Why didn't he hear us?

90
00:04:37.414 --> 00:04:39.115
He went right past the door!"

91
00:04:40.096 --> 00:04:41.477
Waldo slapped his forehead.

92
00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:43.799
"I forgot," he said.

93
00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:47.803
"We could yell all night long, as loud as we can, and nobody would hear us."

94
00:04:47.823 --> 00:04:50.245
"Huh?" said Ben.

95
00:04:50.265 --> 00:04:52.166
"What are you talking about?"

96
00:04:52.186 --> 00:04:58.372
"Mr. Creepy, the science teacher, made the lab soundproof," Waldo explained.

97
00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.182
"He used a magic spell that keeps sound in.

98
00:05:03.123 --> 00:05:07.366
We can hear what's going on outside, but nobody outside can hear what's going on in here."

99
00:05:07.386 --> 00:05:08.907
"Why not?"

100
00:05:09.387 --> 00:05:10.088
asked Ben.

101
00:05:11.689 --> 00:05:12.910
Waldo looked sheepish.

102
00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:19.174
"Last year I was doing an experiment, and I caused a big explosion.

103
00:05:19.974 --> 00:05:23.657
Nobody got hurt, but the explosion disturbed students who were taking the GMAT.

104
00:05:24.497 --> 00:05:27.840
You know, the General Monster Assessment Test that we have to take every spring.

105
00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:31.761
Mr. Freaky was really upset, so he asked Mr.

106
00:05:31.821 --> 00:05:33.742
Creepy to make the science lab soundproof."

107
00:05:35.743 --> 00:05:37.244
Ben blinked in disbelief.

108
00:05:38.064 --> 00:05:40.265
"That means we're stuck in here forever?"

109
00:05:41.465 --> 00:05:42.406
Waldo shrugged.

110
00:05:43.146 --> 00:05:45.127
"Or at least until someone comes to look for us."

111
00:05:46.407 --> 00:05:47.648
He patted Ben on the arm.

112
00:05:47.668 --> 00:05:49.568
"Don't worry.

113
00:05:49.989 --> 00:05:52.630
Our parents will probably start worrying about us by midnight.

114
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:55.571
And we'll definitely be out of here by Monday morning.

115
00:05:56.571 --> 00:05:57.111
That's when Mr.

116
00:05:57.151 --> 00:05:58.172
Creepy comes back to work."

117
00:05:59.236 --> 00:06:00.477
"Monday morning?"

118
00:06:00.837 --> 00:06:01.578
Ben echoed.

119
00:06:02.519 --> 00:06:04.200
He couldn't believe this was happening.

120
00:06:05.101 --> 00:06:07.803
It had taken all of his courage to ask Winnie to the dance.

121
00:06:08.663 --> 00:06:12.687
Now he was stuck in a science lab with Waldo, and he was going to miss the whole

122
00:06:12.767 --> 00:06:13.027
thing!
